## 6. Running the full test suite

After any change to the simulator or plugin, run the suite:

```sh
JOBS=8 bash scripts/run_e2e.sh
```

`JOBS=8` is the practical cap on this 128-core host (vsim Verilator
processes are CPU-hungry; the default cap of 128 saturates the box and
times out). Logs go to `/tmp/e2e-<RAND>/`; failed-test logs are
streamed at the end.

Run a subset:

```sh
FILTER=rt_c_v JOBS=8 bash scripts/run_e2e.sh        # only V-related fixtures
MODE=marker     JOBS=8 bash scripts/run_e2e.sh         # skip the pc-mode iterations
JOBS=1                     bash scripts/run_e2e.sh  # sequential for debugging
LOG_DIR=/tmp/my-logs       bash scripts/run_e2e.sh
VERIFY=1 JOBS=8            bash scripts/run_e2e.sh  # + oracle cross-check per test
```

`VERIFY=1` (default off) adds the differential verification leg to every
test: the fixture re-runs on pure QEMU draining at the ROI exit, and
`andes-sim state-diff` must report zero mismatches against the vsim drain
(see Section 4.7). It needs `build/andes-sim` built.

For a per-mode handoff on the GEMM workload, drive `./andes-sim run`
directly (`--model hybrid --trigger marker|pc|icount`, or `./hsim.py run
--mode simpoint` for SimPoint); see Section 4 for the
mode-by-mode commands.

The e2e suite runs via `scripts/run_e2e.sh`, not CTest; the vsim submodule
registers only the hybrid-layer doctest unit tests (there is no
`switching-mode` CTest label).

